# Files whose bytes are checked, and so must be checked out exactly as committed.
# Git for Windows converts line endings by default (core.autocrlf=true). That would
# change the licence files that font-archives.py compares byte for byte with the
# copies inside the release archives. -text rather than eol=lf: the committed
# licences mix CRLF and LF files, and both must come out unchanged.
/SHA256SUMS -text
/*/licenses/** -text
